# python-gcs — project rules for the agent

## What this is
A MAVLink ground control station. PyQt6 desktop app with a tabbed layout (FLY / PLAN / ANALYTICS / CAMERAS / SETUP).
SIM: PX4 SITL (Gazebo, gz_x500 = the Holybro X500/S500 quad model).
REAL TARGET: Holybro S500 + Pixhawk 6C, which ships with PX4 firmware.
Sim and target firmware MATCH (both PX4). The codebase is PX4-native.

## Stack
- Python 3.9+, PyQt6, raw pymavlink (thread-safe serialization with mav_lock)
- 3D attitude viewer and tactical map are QWebEngineView widgets running three.js /
  Leaflet from local offline tile server / CDN fallbacks. Do NOT add external binary model files.

## File responsibilities
- main.py                  entry point: initializes offline tile server, launches GUI
- gcs/connection.py        connect(conn_str) + request_telemetry (under mav_lock)
- gcs/telemetry.py         per-session pymavlink recv loop -> telemetry_data dict + msg handlers + COMMAND_ACK routing
- gcs/params.py            PX4 INT32/REAL32 byte-wise wire encoding, validation, and diff comparison
- gcs/command_manager.py   correlation of COMMAND_ACK results, progress, timeouts, and state confirmation
- gcs/commands.py          flight commands, OffboardController (10Hz streamer + dead-man timer), mission protocol
- gcs/plan_format.py       standard QGroundControl .plan v1.0 and legacy JSON import/export
- gcs/logs.py              timestamped log buffer
- gcs/telemetry_logger.py  background CSV telemetry logging & in-memory trajectory recorder with GeoJSON/KML export
- gcs/paths.py             asset and font resolution helper
- gcs/ui/gui.py            GCSWindow, ribbon, 3-column layout, flight ribbon, keyboard flight, live 500ms refresh
- gcs/ui/preflight_dialog.py evidence-based pre-flight safety verification (SYS_STATUS sensor health, GNSS, power)
- gcs/ui/survey_dialog.py  aerial survey lawnmower grid generator with altitude propagation
- gcs/ui/setup_view.py     parameter viewer/editor with diff preview, signal-based writes, and readback confirmation
- gcs/ui/map_view.py       Leaflet tactical map (HUD, guided reposition, home position)
- gcs/ui/tile_server.py    local offline HTTP tile server (.png OSM on-demand cache & local MBTiles support)
- gcs/ui/attitude_view.py  Three.js 3D Quad view
- gcs/ui/console_view.py   searchable, categorized MAVLink engineering console
- gcs/ui/camera_view.py    RTSP/MJPEG configurable camera view placeholders

## Conventions — follow these exactly
- vehicle is a pymavlink mavutil connection. Commands send via
  vehicle.mav.*_send / vehicle.mav.send(...). Always serialize all writes under `mav_lock`.
- Log start+end with log().
- GUI button handlers run commands in a daemon thread; never block the Qt main thread.
- Adding telemetry = add key to telemetry_data, add message type to recv filter, add handler, display in refresh().
- refresh() runs on a 500ms QTimer.
- Angles are radians internally, shown in degrees in the UI.
- Style buttons with self._btn_style(color, bg), inputs with _input_style().
  Palette: bg #f5f7fa, panel #ffffff, border #cbd5e1, primary(blue) #0b57d0,
  success(green) #0f9d58, warning(amber) #e37400, danger(red) #d93025,
  muted #5f6368, dark_text #0f172a. Font: Google Sans Code (bundled, SIL OFL).

## PX4 Specifics — do not reuse ArduPilot patterns
- MODES: PX4 modes via pymavlink mode_mapping() include MANUAL, STABILIZED, ALTCTL,
  POSCTL, OFFBOARD, AUTO.LOITER, AUTO.RTL, AUTO.LAND, AUTO.TAKEOFF, AUTO.MISSION.
  There is NO "GUIDED". PX4 custom_mode is bit-packed (main + sub mode), sent via MAV_CMD_DO_SET_MODE.
- OFFBOARD: Requires streaming setpoints (SET_POSITION_TARGET_LOCAL_NED) at >=2 Hz (use 10 Hz)
  with zero velocity for at least 0.5-0.8s BEFORE switching to OFFBOARD.
  Never spoof OFFBOARD mode in GUI before PX4 confirms it.
  Keep streaming setpoints at 10 Hz continuously while in OFFBOARD.
  Implement a dead-man timeout (0.5s): auto-zero velocities to hover if key updates stop.
  Zero velocity on key release, checkbox disable, focus loss, window change, HOLD, RTL, LAND.
- PARAMETERS: PX4 INT32 PARAM_VALUE/PARAM_SET values use byte-wise encoding in the float wire field.
  Decode using struct.unpack('<i', struct.pack('<f', wire_val))[0].
  Encode using struct.unpack('<f', struct.pack('<i', int_val))[0].
  Never optimistically change the displayed/cached value before a matching PARAM_VALUE readback confirms the write.
- MISSIONS: In PX4 MAVLink mission protocol, sequence index 0 is the first uploaded item (e.g. TAKEOFF or first WAYPOINT).
  Do NOT inject Home as sequence 0. Do NOT send mission_clear_all_send before upload; MISSION_COUNT
  atomically replaces the mission upon MISSION_ACK(ACCEPTED). Verify mission count via readback.
- ALTITUDE: GLOBAL_POSITION_INT.relative_alt is altitude relative to home/launch point, NOT terrain AGL.
  Never label launch-relative altitude as AGL unless a true distance sensor (lidar/radar) is available.
- DISARM: Disarming is blocked while vehicle is airborne (EXTENDED_SYS_STATE.landed_state in IN_AIR/TAKEOFF
  or armed with alt > 0.8m). Require explicit emergency confirmation before allowing in-flight disarm.
- HOME: Set home position ONCE when HOME_POSITION message is received or on confirmed initial arm.
  Never call set_home() repeatedly in the refresh loop while armed.
- OSM TILES: OSM Foundation Tile Usage Policy strictly prohibits automated bulk prefetching/scraping.
  Bulk download against tile.openstreetmap.org is disabled. Support local MBTiles files for offline field use.

## How to run / verify
- Sim, headless via Docker:
    docker run --rm -it -p 14540:14540/udp jonasvautherin/px4-gazebo-headless:1.16.1
- Sim, from source: in PX4-Autopilot, `make px4_sitl gz_x500`.
- GCS connects to PX4 offboard/API port over UDP: udpin:0.0.0.0:14540 (or 14550 for QGC).
- Verify all flight behaviors in PX4 SITL. Never test experimental commands on real hardware.
